2026-08-27 - Change Notes:
  - Implement Create Contact and Update Contact, sending requests to Cordial's Contacts API (POST to create, PUT by primary key or by a URI-encoded secondary identifier to update)
  - Generalize the request sender to switch endpoint and HTTP method per event type (orders, contacts, contacts/{identifier}), shared by Order, Create Contact and Update Contact
  - Fix Order event type never firing: the dispatcher checked eventType against a nonexistent "conversion" value instead of the actual "order" value
  - Show the API Key and Use Optimistic Scenario fields for Create Contact and Update Contact, not just Order, since those flows also call the API
  - Restore msID cookie caching on Page View, which had been dropped despite being read back on Order and declared in the template's cookie permissions
  - Extend the send_http permission to allow the new Contacts API endpoints
  - Add unit test coverage for consent/preview early exits, Page View caching, and all Order/Create Contact/Update Contact code paths

